{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.markov_factorising_order_blind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.markov_factorising_order_blind","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.lean#L127-L133","doc":"A Markov-factorising functional is blind to an exchange of the subalgebra it factorises\nover: `τ(θ x · b) = τ(x · b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.dir_diff_same_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.dir_diff_same_sign","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.lean#L107-L119","doc":"If the two channel pieces have opposite signs, `Φ(wP₊) > 0 > Φ(wP₋)`, the corpus-direct\nand difference readings agree in sign on both channels: `P₊` unbound, `P₋` bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.diff_eq_dir_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.diff_eq_dir_iff","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.lean#L94-L99","doc":"The two readings coincide iff the free baseline vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.diff_sub_dir_eq_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.diff_sub_dir_eq_free","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.lean#L90-L92","doc":"Difference reading minus corpus-direct reading is exactly the free baseline. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.diff_eq_neg_dir_complement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.diff_eq_neg_dir_complement","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.lean#L84-L88","doc":"The difference reading of a channel is the negated corpus-direct reading of the\ncomplementary channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.complement_identity_finset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.complement_identity_finset","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.lean#L75-L82","doc":"Finite-family complement identity: `Σ_j P_j = 1 ⟹ Φ w − Φ (w P_i) = Σ_{j ≠ i} Φ (w P_j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.complement_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.complement_identity","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.lean#L69-L73","doc":"Two-channel complement identity: `P + Q = 1 ⟹ Φ w − Φ (w P) = Φ (w Q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.cyclic_conj_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.cyclic_conj_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.lean#L58-L61","doc":"A cyclic functional is invariant under conjugation `x ↦ u x v` with `v u = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.weighted_traces_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.weighted_traces_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaReadingAndExchange.lean#L51-L55","doc":"A weighted sum of cyclic functionals is cyclic. ","signatureChunk":0}]}